"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate explicitly which verify_signature verdict values route to the sign-review-only branch (name each: mismatch, key_not_valid_at_era, invalid, and the wrong-environment foreign_key case), and specify how the ambiguous no-usable-key foreign_key case and the remaining op-cert verdicts (unavailable, unknown_kind, unknown_scheme) are handled — rather than branching only literal `mismatch`.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Full enum (LLM/tool + MCP contract): `verify_signature_result.schema.json:17` = [unsigned, foreign_key, certified, mismatch, key_not_valid_at_era, invalid, unavailable, unknown_kind, unknown_scheme]; also `signing.py:399`.","Persisted-signature verdicts beyond mismatch: `key_not_valid_at_era` (schema: 'a cryptographically-valid signature by a key NOT valid at the event's commit') and `invalid` (op-cert record present but malformed).","`foreign_key` is ambiguous: the wrong-environment branch (`_opcert_verify.py:289-298`) means a signature WAS persisted, but the no-usable-key branch (`_signing_hmac.py:218-224`, `_opcert_verify.py:304-314`) means nothing was signed here — so a blanket route is wrong either way unless disambiguated.","The plan's cited ff4a reason 'ssh-keygen -Y verify rejected signature (exit 255)' is the OP-CERT path, which is exactly the dispatch that emits foreign_key/key_not_valid_at_era/invalid/unavailable/unknown_kind/unknown_scheme — so the omitted verdicts are live on the same code path."],"finding":"AC1's routing set 'any verdict that proves a signature was persisted' is a referenced-but-undefined value vocabulary: the plan branches only the literal verdict `mismatch`, but the signature verdict enum has several other non-certified members that also prove a persisted signature.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb7525a0437d4c5ec","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC1 / section 'The improvement — better than a reorder'","norm_id":"n2979694186d27e6e","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket whose op-cert verifies as `key_not_valid_at_era` or `invalid`: a signature exists, yet the plan routes it to the both-remedies default and still offers the billable `review-plan` as co-equal — the exact defect AC1 set out to fix.","A `foreign_key` verdict from the require_environment / wrong-env branch: a signature was persisted, but sign-review may not resolve it, so neither the mismatch branch nor the both-remedies branch is clearly correct."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define a concrete predicate for 'signature persisted' over the full enum from verify_signature_result.schema.json (e.g. a set {mismatch, key_not_valid_at_era, invalid} plus a disambiguated foreign_key sub-case), and state the fallback remedy for verdicts that do NOT prove persistence (unsigned, no-key foreign_key, unavailable/unknown_kind/unknown_scheme) so every enum member has a defined branch.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the default branch rule explicitly (e.g. 'any verdict other than \"unsigned\" implies a persisted signature → sign-review-only branch; \"unsigned\" → both remedies') or enumerate the verdict values and their branch.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.398,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'When the signature verdict is `mismatch` (or any verdict that proves a signature was persisted)'","AC2 only names 'unsigned' for the both-remedies branch; no full list of possible verdict values is given, so a third verdict's branch is undefined"],"finding":"AC1's parenthetical 'or any verdict that proves a signature was persisted' does not enumerate the verdict domain, leaving the executor to decide which non-mismatch verdicts route to the sign-review-only branch vs. the both-remedies branch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8c6ade35c5ac2c2b","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — AC1 / AC2","norm_id":"nedc44b6f7ce0ebfa","priority":0.402,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A verdict value other than 'mismatch' or 'unsigned' is produced and the executor is unsure which remedy branch it belongs to"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence defining the branch predicate: treat 'unsigned' (no signature persisted) as the both-remedies branch and every other verdict (signature exists) as the sign-review-only branch.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["vague/subjective terms present: better"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the default remedy branch for verdicts other than a signature-proving one and 'unsigned' (which category the else-case joins), and cover that fall-through case in AC3.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'When the signature verdict is `mismatch` (or any verdict that proves a signature was persisted)...'","AC2 handles only 'unsigned'","AC3: 'A test covers both branches by verdict' — 'both' implies exactly two, but AC1's parenthetical implies a category test, not an equality test, so the residual/unknown-verdict case is neither defined nor tested"],"finding":"The plan branches the refusal on result.get('verdict') and tests 'both branches' (mismatch-family vs unsigned), but never specifies the default behaviour for a verdict value that is neither 'unsigned' nor a proof-of-signature (e.g. an empty/missing/unexpected verdict). AC3's 'both branches' leaves that fall-through path unspecified and uncovered, so a verdict the author did not anticipate could silently take whichever branch the code happens to fall into.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f61c63b85f842bebe","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC1 / AC3","norm_id":"n7b73e30eba097c49","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future or unexpected verdict (empty string, a new verdict token) reaches the gate and the refusal shows the wrong remedy — e.g. offering sign-review when no signature exists, or hedging when one does — with no test guarding the choice"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define AC1 as a predicate ('any verdict indicating a persisted signature → sign-review only; all others including unsigned → both remedies') and add a test asserting the else-branch text for an unexpected/empty verdict.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Decide whether `foreign_key` (and any other verdict where a signature was persisted) is in-scope for the sign-review-first branch, and either enumerate those verdicts in AC1/the branch condition or state explicitly why only `mismatch` is covered.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'When the signature verdict is `mismatch` (or any verdict that proves a signature was persisted), the refusal names `rebar sign-review <id>` as THE remedy'","signing.py:399: 'mismatch/foreign_key/unsigned' listed as the produced verdicts","signing.py:250: 'A key-less environment can only ever report unsigned/foreign_key' — foreign_key denotes a persisted signature that failed verification against the current key, i.e. a signature exists"],"finding":"The signing subsystem produces a `foreign_key` verdict (a signature exists but was signed by an unknown/foreign key), which — like `mismatch` — proves a signature was persisted; AC1's parenthetical explicitly scopes the fix to 'any verdict that proves a signature was persisted,' yet the plan enumerates only `mismatch`, so `foreign_key` would fall into the both-remedies branch that offers billable `review-plan` as a co-equal option.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd98ff300ef000ecf","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC1 / src/rebar/signing.py:250,399","norm_id":"n4d23218facb536dd","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:plan-goal-satisfied","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A plan-review attestation was signed by a key not resolvable in the verifying clone's environment: verdict is `foreign_key`, not `mismatch`, so the refusal still offers the billable `review-plan` alongside `sign-review`."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Branch the cheap-remedy message on the set of verdicts that imply a persisted signature (e.g. `verdict in {\"mismatch\", \"foreign_key\"}`) rather than `verdict == \"mismatch\"` alone, and reflect that set in AC1 and AC3's test coverage.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly which verdicts (mismatch and/or foreign_key) route to the sign-review-only branch, so AC1's 'any verdict that proves a signature was persisted' is decided deliberately rather than defaulting foreign_key into the ambiguous both-remedies message.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'When the signature verdict is `mismatch` (or any verdict that proves a signature was persisted)…'","signing.py:399 lists verdicts 'mismatch/foreign_key/unsigned'; signing.py:250 'A key-less environment can only ever report unsigned/foreign_key'","A foreign_key verdict means a signature record exists but was made with a non-matching/foreign key — like mismatch, a signature WAS persisted, so review-plan is not the remedy"],"finding":"AC1 generalizes to 'any verdict that proves a signature was persisted', but the plan only concretely handles 'mismatch' and is silent on the 'foreign_key' verdict, which also proves a signature exists — leaving it in the ambiguous both-remedies branch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb7b496138f47b2d8","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC1","norm_id":"n06c941c5c0417f80","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:plan-goal-satisfied","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket signed under a rotated or foreign key surfaces verdict=foreign_key; the refusal would still offer review-plan (15-20 min, billable) as a co-equal alternative — the exact defect AC1 aims to prevent"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Branch the message on membership in a set of signature-present verdicts (e.g. {\"mismatch\", \"foreign_key\"}) rather than equality with \"mismatch\", and extend AC3 to cover the foreign_key branch.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"dae1720c160fd47c","m